A generic class defines one or more type parameters
like lists, maps. In other words the parameters of these are generic which shows they can be replaced by any non-primitive
java type to create a supposedly new class.
So we can use a list of Strings, list of Integers, list of lists, etc...
when we create an object of a generic class we set concrete parameters. For example:
LinkedList<String> myList = new LinkedList<String>();
HashMap<String,Double> myMap = new HashMap<String,Double>();